       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose of 3,200 mg. You're not a prescriber, so your confirmation doesn't establish that the dose is clinically intended. It also doesn't lower the risk to the patient.\n- **A prescriber has to authorize it.** A finance analyst can't confirm a medication order on a clinician's behalf.\n\n**What can happen next:**\n- The treating prescriber can enter or confirm the order themselves. The pharmacy will probably contact them about the dose.\n- If the prescriber wants a dose within the usual range, such as 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day), I can enter that once they confirm it.\n- If this was a test or a question about the order-entry workflow, I can help with that without placing a real order."
